# EcoDistrict Frontend — Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to .env (never commit .env to version control)
# Vite exposes only variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.

# ── Google Maps / Places API (OPTIONAL) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Used for the "Find Nearby Facilities" feature on the Waste Map page.
#
# ⚠ SECURITY NOTE — this key is NOT a secret:
#   Vite bakes VITE_* variables into the compiled JS bundle at build time.
#   Anyone who opens DevTools can read this key. This is expected and normal
#   for browser-side Google Maps/Places usage.
#   You MUST restrict the key in Google Cloud Console to prevent misuse:
#     1. Application restrictions → HTTP referrers
#        Add:  https://yourdomain.com/*
#              http://localhost:5173/*
#     2. API restrictions → select only:
#        - Maps JavaScript API
#        - Places API
#   An unrestricted key can be used by anyone who finds it in your bundle.
#
# Google Cloud Console setup:
#   1. Create a key at https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis/
#   2. Enable: Maps JavaScript API  +  Places API  (legacy, NOT "Places API New")
#   3. Apply the HTTP referrer and API restrictions above
#   4. Paste the key below in your private .env file — NEVER here
#
# Billing:
#   Google offers a $200/month free credit. The legacy nearbySearch call costs
#   ~$0.032 per call; this app runs 5 calls per search = ~$0.16/search.
#   Keep the key restricted to your domain to avoid unexpected charges.
#
# Fallback:
#   If this key is absent or a Google search fails, the app automatically falls
#   back to OpenStreetMap/Overpass data. The map always works without any key.
#
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Backend API URL (optional override) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Default: Vite dev proxy forwards /api to http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Override only if your backend runs on a different host/port
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
